<title>INDIA: CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA 98 FOR NO WICKET AT LUNCH.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SOUTH AFRICA 98 FOR NO WICKET AT LUNCH.</headline>
<dateline>CALCUTTA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa were 98 without loss at lunch on the first day of the second cricket test against India at Eden Gardens on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Batting first after winning the toss, South Africa's openers Andrew Hudson and Gary Kirsten were unbeaten on 41 and 50, respectively, after 29 overs.</p>
